[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Audio Playback Low Level Software Requirements
UID: YAAP-APLLSR
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: APLLSR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the low level software requirements for Yet Another 
Audio Player (Yaap), a time accurate desktop audio player.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: File Handling

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: File Type Identification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-001
TITLE: Format and Encoding Identification
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall identify an input audio stream's format and encoding.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-002
TITLE: Supported Format Detection
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall determine whether an input audio stream's identified format 
and encoding are supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-003
TITLE: Unsupported Format Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an unsupported-format error when an input audio
stream's format is unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-004
TITLE: Unsupported Encoding Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an unsupported-encoding error when an input audio
stream's encoding is unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-005
TITLE: Unknown Format Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an unknown-format error when an input audio
stream's format is unknown.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-006
TITLE: Unknown Encoding Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an unknown-encoding error when an input audio
stream's encoding is unknown.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-007
TITLE: Invalid Format Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an invalid-format error when an input audio
stream's format is invalid.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-008
TITLE: Invalid Encoding Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an invalid-encoding error when an input audio
stream's encoding is invalid.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-009
TITLE: No Audio Track Detection
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall detect when an input audio stream contains no audio tracks.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-010
TITLE: FLAC Encoding Identification
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall identify whether an input audio stream is encoded in the 
FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-011
TITLE: FLAC Identification Independent of Extension
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall identify FLAC audio streams independently from the stream's 
filename extension.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Stream Metadata Retrieval

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-012
TITLE: FLAC Channel Count Extraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall obtain the channel count from the FLAC stream's metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-013
TITLE: Invalid FLAC Channel Count Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an Invalid Channel Count Error when validation 
determines that the channel count retrieved from a FLAC stream is outside the 
range permitted by the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-014
TITLE: FLAC Sample Rate Extraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall obtain the sample rate from the FLAC stream's metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-015
TITLE: Invalid FLAC Sample Rate Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an Invalid Sample Rate Error when validation 
determines that the sample rate retrieved from a FLAC stream is outside the 
range permitted by the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-016
TITLE: FLAC Bits per Sample Extraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall obtain the bits per sample from the FLAC stream's metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-017
TITLE: Invalid Bits per Sample Error Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate an Invalid Bits Per Sample Error when validation 
determines that the bits per sample value retrieved from a FLAC stream is 
outside the range permitted by the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-018
TITLE: FLAC Sample Accurate Duration Calculation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall calculate the duration of a FLAC stream using its total
sample count and sample rate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-019
TITLE: FLAC Duration Calculation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall calculate the duration of a FLAC stream using its time base 
and tick count if it cannot be calculated using the total sample count and
sample rate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: APLLSR-020
TITLE: FLAC Unknown Duration Handling
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall indicate that the duration of a FLAC stream is unknown when 
neither the total sample count and sample rate nor the time base and tick
count required to calculate the duration are available.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APHLSR-008

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]
